WEBVTT

00:02.135 --> 00:03.602
Legend has it that...

00:04.771 --> 00:07.569
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:07.908 --> 00:13.244
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.714 --> 00:19.879
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:32.999 --> 00:40.428
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.707 --> 00:46.543
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.081 --> 00:53.986
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.655 --> 00:59.421
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.526 --> 01:02.723
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.500 --> 01:13.565
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.740 --> 01:19.576
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.447 --> 01:27.717
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:27.888 --> 01:36.296
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:36.997 --> 01:38.658
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.408 --> 01:51.844
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:57.918 --> 02:00.352
<i>Mikuni Maru</i>

02:00.520 --> 02:03.819
At Saigo's urging, Ryoma Sakamoto,
injured in the Teradaya Incident...

02:04.090 --> 02:07.924
...is on his way to get some rest at
the Kirishima hot springs in Satsuma...

02:08.061 --> 02:10.291
...taking O-Ryo with him.

02:10.864 --> 02:15.563
It is the first honeymoon
ever taken in Japan.

02:16.269 --> 02:18.100
A trip to celebrate your marriage?

02:19.339 --> 02:20.237
That's right...

02:20.373 --> 02:26.107
Katsu-Sensei once told me that it's
what they do in Western cultures.

02:26.546 --> 02:30.141
When a man and woman marry, they
go off on a trip to see the sights.

02:30.317 --> 02:32.012
So that's what this trip is about?

02:32.686 --> 02:34.483
Looks like it is.

02:39.526 --> 02:41.153
Ever since the incident at Teradaya...

02:41.294 --> 02:43.854
...O-Ryo has gone out of
her way to take care of me.

02:44.064 --> 02:45.531
The rest just happened.

02:45.665 --> 02:47.064
I guess it can't be helped, then.

02:47.234 --> 02:48.565
Cha, cha, cha!

02:49.135 --> 02:51.569
You shouldn't stand in the
sea breeze for too long.

02:51.705 --> 02:53.673
It's not good for your wound.

02:55.108 --> 02:57.975
But I don't like staying
cooped up below deck.

02:58.211 --> 03:01.146
Are you saying you
don't like my company?

03:02.582 --> 03:06.018
We just got married, how
could I not like your company?

03:07.487 --> 03:10.354
And anyway, if you and I
stayed downstairs together...

03:10.490 --> 03:13.323
...who knows what everybody
else will start thinking!

03:14.361 --> 03:17.455
And if that happened, the whole
ship could get steered off course...

03:17.597 --> 03:19.895
...and there'd be a disaster!

03:20.033 --> 03:21.466
You really think so?

03:21.568 --> 03:23.058
Yes, absolutely!

03:32.045 --> 03:35.879
Looks like you're the one having
trouble with the sea breeze!

03:36.149 --> 03:37.548
Not at all!

03:38.118 --> 03:39.745
It's troubling to us, though.

03:39.853 --> 03:40.478
Yeah!

03:43.990 --> 03:48.654
<i>The Dragon Incarnate</i>

03:55.802 --> 04:00.501
Hey, listen. I'm thinking of
climbing Mt. Kirishima tomorrow.

04:00.740 --> 04:01.900
You ready for that?

04:02.609 --> 04:04.873
The wound's all healed now.

04:07.614 --> 04:13.382
The innkeeper told me that at
Takachiho, the top of Kirishima...

04:13.586 --> 04:16.646
...there's something
called a Heavenly Sakahoko...

04:16.790 --> 04:20.817
...a spear driven upside
down into the ground by a god...

04:21.027 --> 04:22.460
That sounds strange...

04:22.595 --> 04:24.153
I'd like to see it, too.

04:24.664 --> 04:26.689
You will take me with you?

04:27.200 --> 04:31.159
Kirishima's a tough mountain
to climb, even for a man.

04:31.604 --> 04:33.799
I'll be quite all right!

04:33.973 --> 04:36.441
I may not look it, but
I've got strong legs.

04:42.449 --> 04:45.976
<i>Kirishima</i>

05:00.400 --> 05:01.128
Whoops!

05:05.238 --> 05:06.432
Are you all right?

05:09.442 --> 05:10.932
Let's stay this way.

05:15.482 --> 05:16.471
Sure.

05:24.023 --> 05:25.957
"The rest just happened," huh?

05:45.545 --> 05:48.537
Legend has it that at
the beginning of time...

05:48.681 --> 05:51.775
...a god drove this spear into the ground
when he descended to this mountain...

05:51.918 --> 05:54.443
It's a lot smaller than
I thought it would be...

05:55.121 --> 05:57.919
That's how it is with all
the gimmicks of the world.

05:58.057 --> 06:02.050
Someone, somewhere created this
myth to blow his own horn, see...

06:02.195 --> 06:03.321
Hmm...

06:03.596 --> 06:05.791
But if you get up close and
see it with your own eyes...

06:05.899 --> 06:07.867
...you can see it for what it really is.

06:08.001 --> 06:11.596
It's a lot like the Bakufu
and the Shogun, you know...

06:17.744 --> 06:20.611
O-Ryo, try pulling the Sakahoko out.

06:20.713 --> 06:21.509
What?

06:34.727 --> 06:37.594
I wonder if it was placed
here by the gods, after all?

06:37.764 --> 06:40.062
It was placed there by humans!

06:57.383 --> 07:00.079
I didn't think it would even budge, but...

07:00.453 --> 07:02.717
It might not have been
removed by a human...

07:02.889 --> 07:04.186
Izumi!

07:04.591 --> 07:07.059
You were able to remove it
because you're Ryoma Sakamoto...

07:07.260 --> 07:08.887
There's no question about it.

07:11.164 --> 07:11.960
Here!

07:21.875 --> 07:24.469
No human could pull
off that trick, either!

07:24.944 --> 07:29.938
Now no one but Ryoma Sakamoto can
ever withdraw this spear again.

07:32.719 --> 07:37.486
Perhaps these two... aren't
really human, after all!

07:37.857 --> 07:39.984
Why don't we just leave it at that, okay?

07:40.960 --> 07:42.257
Come on, let's go.

07:43.696 --> 07:47.792
There are more tasks that can only be
accomplished by Ryoma Sakamoto!

07:54.240 --> 07:55.571
Whoa!

07:56.976 --> 07:58.944
Forgive me, O-Ryo...

07:59.646 --> 08:01.876
It looks like our vacation's over.

08:05.785 --> 08:12.349
In the days that followed, Ryoma's
achievements would earn him the...

08:12.825 --> 08:16.158
...reputation of being
a dragon incarnate...

08:16.396 --> 08:21.095
...sent from heaven to take
control in a turbulent era.

08:22.702 --> 08:25.398
<i>Sakurajima</i>

08:25.672 --> 08:29.699
<i>Union-Gou</i>

08:31.144 --> 08:33.806
Saigo's more stubborn than I thought.

08:34.147 --> 08:35.478
You said it!

08:36.983 --> 08:39.713
There's no way we can accept this.

08:40.153 --> 08:42.519
But Saigo, these 500
koku of rice were...

08:42.622 --> 08:45.682
...given as an act of goodwill,
in honor of the alliance.

08:46.259 --> 08:49.626
For the last few years, Satsuma
has been plagued by crop failure...

08:49.762 --> 08:52.128
...while Choshu has abundant rice.

08:52.298 --> 08:54.698
It won't do to reject such an offering.

08:54.834 --> 08:57.359
We can't take it because
it's an act of goodwill!

08:58.171 --> 09:00.799
You know this as well as I do,
Sakamoto.

09:01.474 --> 09:04.443
The Shogunate is sending
troops to subjugate Choshu.

09:04.644 --> 09:08.080
The people of Choshu, even
the farmers and townsfolk...

09:08.214 --> 09:12.116
...are all taking up arms
to meet them in battle.

09:12.652 --> 09:17.988
Right now, it's not Satsuma that
needs provisions, but Choshu.

09:18.458 --> 09:21.222
Don't you see that, Sakamoto?

09:21.894 --> 09:23.885
I know what you're saying...

09:24.097 --> 09:26.998
...still, is there any
way you could just take it?

09:27.333 --> 09:28.664
No, there isn't!

09:28.935 --> 09:30.732
There isn't a single man in Satsuma...

09:30.837 --> 09:33.567
...who would be happy taking
rice from another domain in need!

09:33.873 --> 09:36.205
It's true, Choshu is strapped for food.

09:36.643 --> 09:38.907
But they sent all this
despite their own need.

09:39.112 --> 09:42.081
That's why you're only going
to offend them by rejecting it.

09:42.248 --> 09:43.772
It'll rub them the wrong way.

09:44.317 --> 09:47.548
I mean, what's the point of the
Satsuma-Choshu Alliance, then?

09:48.588 --> 09:52.422
That's why I'm turning to you,
the man who created the alliance!

09:52.659 --> 09:55.321
I'm asking you to send
this rice back to Choshu...

09:55.428 --> 09:58.090
...and make sure no
feathers are ruffled.

09:58.197 --> 09:59.494
Oh, man!

10:01.501 --> 10:03.765
If you don't play your cards right...

10:03.870 --> 10:06.430
...the entire Satsuma-Choshu
Alliance could be jeopardized.

10:06.539 --> 10:07.665
I know.

10:07.874 --> 10:09.865
Even so, you're not worried.

10:09.976 --> 10:11.307
Cha, cha, cha!

10:11.844 --> 10:14.608
You pulled out the Sakahoko...

10:14.781 --> 10:18.148
...there's nothing that
Ryo Sakamoto can't do.

10:20.386 --> 10:27.349
Meanwhile, the four warships sent by
the Shogunate to subjugate Choshu...

10:27.727 --> 10:32.858
...sit moored in Yashima Bay,
off Oshima, in the Setouchi Sea.

10:33.733 --> 10:35.535
A single ship under the command...

10:35.535 --> 10:35.668
<i>Hei-In Maru</i>
A single ship under the command...

10:35.668 --> 10:38.535
<i>Hei-In Maru</i>
...of Shinsaku Takasugi of Choshu...

10:38.905 --> 10:41.931
...has arrived to meet
the Shogunate's attack.

10:46.946 --> 10:49.141
The enemy has its guard down
completely.

10:49.549 --> 10:50.777
Now's our chance.

10:51.851 --> 10:52.579
Fire!

10:55.621 --> 10:56.417
Fire!

10:56.556 --> 10:57.921
Fire at will!

11:06.099 --> 11:08.659
We're being attacked by a
huge battleship from Choshu!

11:08.968 --> 11:10.367
Pull up the anchor!

11:11.504 --> 11:13.096
We're retreating for now!

11:33.426 --> 11:34.293
<i>Bakan Choshu Residence</i>

11:34.293 --> 11:36.853
<i>Bakan Choshu Residence</i>
So that's the story, Katsura.

11:37.396 --> 11:40.365
Will you take back the 500 koku of rice?

11:40.800 --> 11:43.792
Because Satsuma has
taken pity on Choshu?

11:45.071 --> 11:49.405
Cha, cha, cha! You've got
the wrong idea, Katsura.

11:52.979 --> 11:56.415
I wasn't going to tell you
this, but I have no choice.

11:58.351 --> 12:00.945
You can't tell anybody, got that?

12:01.387 --> 12:04.379
Saigo actually shed tears of gratitude!

12:04.557 --> 12:06.024
You mean Saigo cried?

12:07.093 --> 12:10.028
Oh, yes, that huge body of
his was heaving with sobs...

12:10.129 --> 12:12.962
...and the tears were pouring down...

12:13.099 --> 12:13.929
Whoops!

12:14.500 --> 12:15.899
I've said too much now!

12:17.804 --> 12:22.366
It was really killing him that
he couldn't accept your rice.

12:22.809 --> 12:26.905
But he said if he took rice from Choshu
just as it was about to go into battle...

12:27.046 --> 12:29.844
...he couldn't live with himself.

12:31.284 --> 12:32.444
All right, then.

12:32.652 --> 12:34.210
I knew you'd get it, Katsura!

12:34.387 --> 12:37.185
No, I myself "get" it...

12:37.590 --> 12:41.458
But this rice was officially requisitioned
from the Choshu reserves.

12:41.761 --> 12:43.991
The domain can't possibly take it back...

12:44.197 --> 12:48.190
Come on, who cares? So long
as you're not offended, Katsura...

12:48.334 --> 12:50.165
But Sakamoto, the rice...

12:50.903 --> 12:52.097
The rice?

12:52.839 --> 12:55.205
I'll be more than
happy to take it myself!

12:55.308 --> 12:56.240
You?

12:56.576 --> 12:58.976
It's like they say in Ooka Sabaki...

12:59.212 --> 13:01.874
"All 3 parties lose the
same amount of money."

13:02.014 --> 13:03.276
But, don't you see, that rice...

13:03.382 --> 13:07.512
Right! It's a loss for Satsuma not to
accept rice that was offered to them.

13:07.720 --> 13:11.451
A loss for Choshu, since
you're out 500 koku of rice.

13:11.591 --> 13:13.081
And as for me...

13:13.326 --> 13:15.157
You're the only one
who's gained anything.

13:15.261 --> 13:17.559
Hey, that's right!
Didn't think of that!

13:17.697 --> 13:19.460
I can't believe I missed that!

13:19.966 --> 13:22.059
So, does that work for you?

13:30.643 --> 13:33.578
I guess I don't stand
a chance against you!

13:34.447 --> 13:36.813
All right, I'll just eat this loss.

13:36.983 --> 13:39.178
To be precise, it's not really a loss.

13:40.953 --> 13:42.614
"Everybody Wins"...

13:42.755 --> 13:45.417
That's the upshot of this Rice Incident.

13:46.192 --> 13:48.786
Ryoma wins because he
gains 500 koku of rice.

13:48.928 --> 13:51.590
Saigo also wins because he's able to...

13:51.697 --> 13:53.562
...save face by not
accepting rice from Choshu.

13:53.666 --> 13:56.157
And exactly what kind of
gain has our domain made?

13:56.969 --> 13:59.904
At a mere cost of 500
koku, you can save Choshu.

14:00.206 --> 14:01.639
You win big!

14:02.875 --> 14:07.209
Or were you actually planning
to work for free, Ryoma?

14:07.346 --> 14:08.973
Cha, cha, cha!

14:12.418 --> 14:14.943
Takasugi! So you've returned?

14:15.755 --> 14:18.121
Sakamoto, I have a favor to ask of you.

14:19.158 --> 14:23.561
Will you consider joining us in our
fight against the Shogunate's Navy?

14:31.270 --> 14:32.396
Takasugi!

14:33.039 --> 14:37.874
About that, I think I've
already arranged that for you.

14:39.245 --> 14:42.146
Two days ago, in the
middle of the night...

14:42.315 --> 14:45.307
...we met the Shogunate Navy
for the first time off Oshima.

14:45.418 --> 14:47.909
Under cover of darkness, we
caught the enemy off guard...

14:48.087 --> 14:51.284
...and managed to force
the squadron into retreat.

14:54.727 --> 14:57.560
Cha, cha, cha!
That's really impressive!

14:57.797 --> 14:58.525
No.

14:58.631 --> 15:02.328
We were only able to pull it off because
of their carelessness and low morale.

15:02.468 --> 15:05.164
This much was clear when
we met them in battle...

15:05.471 --> 15:09.908
...the Shogunate Navy is much
stronger than our Choshu Navy.

15:10.076 --> 15:11.475
Well, that's no surprise.

15:11.544 --> 15:12.408
So?

15:12.878 --> 15:17.144
The Shogunate fleet will be attacking
the Bakan Strait from four directions.

15:17.683 --> 15:21.119
But the Shogunate fleet is
still moored in Oshima Bay...

15:21.687 --> 15:23.678
...so that's where
my ship comes in, huh?

15:23.856 --> 15:24.584
Right.

15:24.690 --> 15:27.124
Our plan is to have the Union...

15:27.259 --> 15:30.922
...and our Choshu fleet bombard their
artillery before they can attack.

15:32.431 --> 15:36.094
In the meantime, our brigade
will destroy the artillery...

15:36.235 --> 15:39.227
...and take over the Shogunate
headquarters at Ogura Castle.

15:39.872 --> 15:43.364
The outcome of the war will
be determined by this strategy!

15:44.577 --> 15:45.839
You're putting your lives on the line.

15:50.049 --> 15:51.141
Right, then!

15:51.250 --> 15:54.651
The Union crew and I are ready to
risk our lives along with you!

15:54.787 --> 15:56.118
Right!

16:23.249 --> 16:25.945
The mist is absolutely perfect...

16:27.186 --> 16:28.710
Let's get right to it!

16:28.854 --> 16:29.252
Right!

16:41.767 --> 16:44.565
So that's the Shogunate's artillery?

16:45.471 --> 16:46.995
No time to lose, all right?

16:47.173 --> 16:48.936
Let's open our assault!

16:49.041 --> 16:49.735
Right!

16:50.042 --> 16:51.976
Open fire!

17:02.621 --> 17:04.179
Now, men! Charge!

17:11.664 --> 17:13.928
It's a sneak attack! Return fire!

17:14.366 --> 17:15.958
Fire! Fire!

17:31.283 --> 17:32.750
Cha, cha, cha!

17:32.918 --> 17:35.318
Looks like we finally woke
up the Shogunate forces!

17:36.055 --> 17:38.455
I wonder how Takasugi and
his men are holding up?

17:39.525 --> 17:41.925
Okay, I'll be off, then.

17:43.062 --> 17:44.689
Where are you going?

17:53.939 --> 17:56.339
What on earth is Lord
Mutsu planning to do?

17:56.542 --> 17:58.169
Nothing to worry about.

17:58.310 --> 17:59.937
See, he's no human...

18:00.045 --> 18:01.376
He's a demon!

18:01.514 --> 18:02.481
Oh...

18:13.459 --> 18:14.255
Dammit!

18:15.394 --> 18:17.055
At this rate...

18:17.229 --> 18:18.253
Commander Takasugi...

18:18.564 --> 18:21.294
We'll infiltrate the compound,
and destroy the artillery.

18:21.467 --> 18:22.331
What?

18:24.036 --> 18:26.334
Their defenses are
thin on the other side.

18:26.472 --> 18:27.404
It's too risky!

18:28.274 --> 18:31.732
We've already put our lives
in your hands, Commander!

18:36.115 --> 18:39.482
Then, I order you to
destroy the artillery.

18:39.652 --> 18:40.641
Yes, sir!

18:55.000 --> 18:56.228
That's their powder shed.

19:10.316 --> 19:11.442
Don't move!

19:16.689 --> 19:17.986
Our number's up...

19:18.123 --> 19:20.785
Then all that's left to do
is to kill as many as we can!

19:20.893 --> 19:24.590
Firing guns in a place like this?
Think of the danger!

19:26.498 --> 19:30.832
If this thing were to be ignited, I
bet there'd be some serious fireworks!

19:34.607 --> 19:35.665
Who the hell are you?

19:35.774 --> 19:37.105
Doesn't matter! Fire!

19:40.412 --> 19:41.879
Fire! Fire!

19:49.321 --> 19:50.413
Now's our chance!

19:59.965 --> 20:01.057
Bastards!

20:11.710 --> 20:13.610
We can't thank you
enough for your help...

20:13.779 --> 20:15.713
Let's do it before the
reinforcements get here!

20:20.853 --> 20:23.321
Fire! Just keep firing away!

20:24.323 --> 20:26.723
Lord Sakamoto, at this rate, I'm afraid...

20:26.959 --> 20:28.893
Hey, just sit back and watch.

20:29.028 --> 20:30.518
You'll see, soon enough...

20:40.739 --> 20:43.139
Now! Storm the artillery!

20:54.186 --> 20:55.175
Look at that.

20:55.287 --> 20:56.015
Yes...

20:56.322 --> 21:00.486
The Choshu brigade is made up of
nothing but farmers and townsmen...

21:00.759 --> 21:04.889
...yet they're putting up such a valiant
fight against the Shogun's troops.

21:05.831 --> 21:08.959
Victory is ours today!

21:17.476 --> 21:20.445
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.623 --> 21:43.660
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:43.936 --> 21:53.675
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.812 --> 22:02.811
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:02.955 --> 22:13.627
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.666 --> 22:20.798
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.173 --> 22:24.165
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.043 --> 22:31.312
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.617 --> 22:37.112
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:51.737 --> 22:53.705
So now you're going to counterattack...

22:53.806 --> 22:56.832
...the Shogunate's Navy with
a single ship, the Union?

22:56.942 --> 22:58.739
Sounds like fun, Ryoma!

22:59.878 --> 23:01.812
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:01.914 --> 23:03.381
<i>Battle in the Dark</i>

23:03.515 --> 23:05.745
Pay close attention, and wait!
